problem:
Problem description
- There is a single-period production planning problem with a product set $$P$$ indexed by $$p \in P$$, and a planning horizon $$\mathcal{T}$$ with $$\lvert \mathcal{T} \rvert = 1$$.
- Each product $$p \in P$$ has a unit profit $$\pi_p$$, a wood requirement per unit $$a^{\mathrm{wood}}_p$$, and a steel requirement per unit $$a^{\mathrm{steel}}_p$$.
- The manufacturer has total available wood $$W$$ and total available steel $$S$$.
- The planning goal is to choose which product types to manufacture and how many units of each selected product to produce so that total profit is maximized.
- Production quantities are nonnegative integers, and each product type is either manufactured or not manufactured.
- The available wood and steel must not be exceeded by the total production plan.
- If a product type is not selected for manufacture, its production quantity must be zero.
- If a product type is selected, its production quantity must be compatible with the available resource limits.
- The logical business rules are:
  - if the truck product type is manufactured, the train product type must not be manufactured;
  - if the boat product type is manufactured, the airplane product type must also be manufactured;
  - the number of boats produced cannot exceed the number of trains produced.
- A solution is represented by:
  - $$x_p$$: the integer number of units produced of product $$p \in P$$;
  - $$y_p$$: a binary indicator showing whether product $$p \in P$$ is manufactured;
  - $$K$$: the number of product types that are manufactured.

Input Format
{
  "products": {
    "symbol": "$$P$$",
    "type": "array of product identifiers",
    "description": "The set of product types indexed by $$p \in P$$"
  },
  "unit_profit": {
    "symbol": "$$\\pi_p$$",
    "shape": "[$$|P|$$]",
    "type": "array of numbers",
    "description": "Unit profit for each product $$p \\in P$$"
  },
  "wood_capacity": {
    "symbol": "$$W$$",
    "type": "number",
    "description": "Total available wood"
  },
  "wood_requirement": {
    "symbol": "$$a^{\\mathrm{wood}}_p$$",
    "shape": "[$$|P|$$]",
    "type": "array of numbers",
    "description": "Wood required per unit of product $$p \\in P$$"
  },
  "steel_capacity": {
    "symbol": "$$S$$",
    "type": "number",
    "description": "Total available steel"
  },
  "steel_requirement": {
    "symbol": "$$a^{\\mathrm{steel}}_p$$",
    "shape": "[$$|P|$$]",
    "type": "array of numbers",
    "description": "Steel required per unit of product $$p \\in P$$"
  },
  "market_demand": {
    "symbol": "$$D_p$$",
    "shape": "[$$|P|$$]",
    "type": "optional array of numbers",
    "description": "Maximum sellable quantity for each product $$p \\in P$$; if omitted, no separate demand cap is imposed"
  },
  "forbidden_pairs": {
    "symbol": "$$\\mathcal{F}$$",
    "type": "array of ordered pairs",
    "description": "Pairs $$(p,q)$$ such that manufacturing $$p$$ prohibits manufacturing $$q$$"
  },
  "implication_pairs": {
    "symbol": "$$\\mathcal{I}$$",
    "type": "array of ordered pairs",
    "description": "Pairs $$(p,q)$$ such that manufacturing $$p$$ requires manufacturing $$q$$"
  },
  "quantity_ordering_pairs": {
    "symbol": "$$\\mathcal{R}$$",
    "type": "array of ordered pairs",
    "description": "Pairs $$(p,q)$$ such that the production quantity of $$p$$ cannot exceed the production quantity of $$q$$"
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "production_quantity": {
    "symbol": "$$x_p$$",
    "shape": "[$$|P|$$]",
    "type": "array of integers",
    "description": "Optimal production quantity for each product $$p \\in P$$"
  },
  "manufacture_indicator": {
    "symbol": "$$y_p$$",
    "shape": "[$$|P|$$]",
    "type": "array of binary values",
    "description": "Whether product $$p \\in P$$ is manufactured"
  },
  "manufactured_type_count": {
    "symbol": "$$K$$",
    "type": "integer",
    "description": "Number of product types selected for manufacture"
  },
  "total_profit": {
    "symbol": "$$Z^*$$",
    "type": "number",
    "description": "Maximum achievable total profit"
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "products": ["truck", "airplane", "boat", "train"],
  "unit_profit": [5, 10, 8, 7],
  "wood_capacity": 890,
  "wood_requirement": [12, 20, 15, 10],
  "steel_capacity": 500,
  "steel_requirement": [6, 3, 5, 4],
  "forbidden_pairs": [["truck", "train"]],
  "implication_pairs": [["boat", "airplane"]],
  "quantity_ordering_pairs": [["boat", "train"]]
}
